{"step_index":85,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T04:24:27Z","model":"gpt-oss-120b-medium","input_tokens":15729,"cache_read_tokens":31523,"output_tokens":1129,"thinking":"Now need to implement manage-products.js, manage-orders.js, reports.js.\n\nImplement logic per requirements.\n\nNeed to handle edit/delete/updating status.\n\nBecause we are only required to implement page-specific JS; HTML already there.\n\nImplement manage-products.js:\n\n- Verify seller login.\n- Load seller's products list, each product displayed with edit/delete buttons, status, rejection remarks.\n- Edit: open a simple inline form or prompt; we can use `prompt` for simplicity.\n- Delete: confirm via `confirm`.\n- Update product details: name, description, price, stock, image URL, category.\n- Save back to storage.\n\nImplement manage-orders.js:\n\n- Load orders where items contain sellerId of logged-in seller.\n- For each order, show order ID, date, customer name, product name(s), quantity, status.\n- Provide button to advance status: statuses are Placed -> Packed -> Shipped -> Delivered.\n- Update order.deliveryStatus accordingly and persist.\n\nImplement reports.js (simple placeholder but can compute total revenue and number of orders for this seller).\n\nImplement UI interactions with minimal prompts.\n\nWill need to access users to get customer name via userId.\n\nLet's code.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"// manage-products.js – list, edit, delete seller's own products\n(function(){\n    const storage = window.StorageAPI;\n    const sess = storage.getSession();\n    if(!sess || sess.role!=='seller'){\n        alert('Please log in as a seller');\n        window.location.href='../login.html';\n        return;\n    }\n    const products = storage.get(storage.keys.products) || [];\n    const myProducts = products.filter(p=>p.sellerId===sess.userId);\n    const container = document.getElementById('productsList');\n    if(myProducts.length===0){\n        container.innerHTML = '<p>You have no products yet.</p>';\n        return;\n    }\n    myProducts.forEach(p=>{\n        const card = document.createElement('div');\n        card.className='card';\n        card.innerHTML = `\n            <h3>${p.name}</h3>\n            <p><strong>Category:</strong> ${getCategoryName(p.categoryId)}</p>\n            <p><strong>Price:</strong> ₹${p.price.toFixed(2)}</p>\n            <p><strong>Stock:</strong> ${p.stock}</p>\n            <p><strong>Status:</strong> ${p.status}</p>\n            ${p.status==='rejected' ? `<p><strong>Remark:</strong> ${p.rejectionRemarks || '—'}</p>` : ''}\n            <button class=\"btn editBtn\" data-id=\"${p.id}\">Edit</button>\n            <button class=\"btn deleteBtn\" data-id=\"${p.id}\">Delete</button>\n        `;\n        container.appendChild(card);\n    });\n\n    // helper to map category id to name\n    function getCategoryName(catId){\n        const cat = (storage.get(storage.keys.categories)||[]).find(c=>c.id===catId);\n        return cat ? cat.name : '';\n    }\n\n    // Edit flow – simple prompts for each field\n    container.addEventListener('click', function(e){\n        if(e.target.classList.contains('editBtn')){\n            const pid = e.target.dataset.id;\n            const product = products.find(p=>p.id===pid);\n            if(!product) return;\n            const newName = prompt('Product name:', product.name) || product.name;\n            const newDesc = prompt('Description:', product.description) || product.description;\n            const newPrice = parseFloat(prompt('Price (₹):', product.price));\n            const newStock = parseInt(prompt('Stock quantity:', product.stock));\n            const newImg = prompt('Image URL:', product.image) || product.image;\n            const newCatId = prompt('Category ID (use existing IDs):', product.categoryId) || product.categoryId;\n            // Basic validation\n            if(isNaN(newPrice) || isNaN(newStock)){\n                alert('Invalid number entered. Edit cancelled.');\n                return;\n            }\n            product.name = newName.trim();\n            product.description = newDesc.trim();\n            product.price = newPrice;\n            product.stock = newStock;\n            product.image = newImg.trim();\n            product.categoryId = newCatId;\n            // keep status as is (cannot become approved)\n            storage.set(storage.keys.products, products);\n            alert('Product updated.');\n            location.reload();\n        }\n        if(e.target.classList.contains('deleteBtn')){\n            const pid = e.target.dataset.id;\n            if(confirm('Delete this product? This cannot be undone.')){\n                const idx = products.findIndex(p=>p.id===pid);\n                if(idx>-1){\n                    products.splice(idx,1);\n                    storage.set(storage.keys.products, products);\n                    alert('Product deleted.');\n                    location.reload();\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    });\n})();"}}]}
