{"step_index":91,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T04:24:44Z","model":"gpt-oss-120b-medium","input_tokens":1232,"cache_read_tokens":48174,"output_tokens":1283,"thinking":"We need to continue implementing seller workflow: add manage-orders.js and reports.js. Also possibly fix any missing imports in HTML (include correct scripts). Need to ensure seller pages use relative paths appropriately.\n\nAlso verify that `seller/` folder existed before; it was empty earlier. Now we have pages and JS.\n\nNow add `manage-orders.js` script to display orders containing seller's products, allow status updates through dropdown.\n\nImplement simple status progression.\n\nAdd `reports.js` script can show placeholder summary (e.g., total revenue, number orders). Should compute from orders containing seller's items.\n\nAlso need to ensure `assets/js/main.js` navigation works for seller pages (role detection). Should be fine.\n\nPotential minor issue: In `manage-products.js` there is stray `n` after storage.getSession() (typo introduced). It currently reads:\n\n```\nconst sess = storage.getSession();n    if(!sess...\n```\n\nWe need to remove stray `n`. Let's edit file to correct.\n\nAlso ensure that the edit-script uses correct property names: in storage.js product property `sellerId` is stored as 'sellerId', while session property is `userId`. In previous code we used `sess.userId`. However we assigned `id` property as 'u-...' in storage seed. In auth session we set `userId: user.id`. Good.\n\nBut in some code we referenced `sess.sellerId` incorrectly? Actually in dashboard.js we used `sess.userId`. Good.\n\nIn `manage-products.js` we use `sess.userId` when filtering `p.sellerId===sess.userId`. That is correct.\n\nNow implement `manage-orders.js`:\n\n- Get session.\n- Filter orders where any item.sellerId===session.userId.\n- Show each order: order ID, date, customer name (need to fetch from users), product list (only those belonging to seller?), quantity, status.\n- Provide a dropdown to change status (Placed > Packed > Shipped > Delivered). Only allow forward progression maybe.\n\nSimplify: For each order, show current deliveryStatus, a select with options, and a button to save.\n\nImplement update: modify order.deliveryStatus, store back, and show toast.\n\nCreate `manage-orders.js`.\n\nAlso add `reports.js`:\n\n- Compute total revenue: sum of order items where sellerId matches and order status not cancelled? For simplicity sum all subTotal values for items belonging to seller.\n\n- Count total orders.\n\n- Show figure.\n\nNow we need to create these JS files.\n\nAlso fix navigation: seller pages include `../assets/js/main.js` which builds navbar; that script already loads `buildNav` and role detection.\n\nNow we need to edit `seller/manage-orders.html` includes script `manage-orders.js`.\n\nImplement.\n\nNow create files.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"// manage-orders.js – seller view of orders containing their products & status updates\n(function(){\n    const storage = window.StorageAPI;\n    const sess = storage.getSession();\n    if(!sess || sess.role!=='seller'){\n        alert('Please log in as a seller');\n        window.location.href='../login.html';\n        return;\n    }\n    const orders = storage.get(storage.keys.orders) || [];\n    const users = storage.get(storage.keys.users) || [];\n    const sellerOrders = orders.filter(o=>o.items.some(it=>it.sellerId===sess.userId));\n    const container = document.getElementById('ordersList');\n\n    if(sellerOrders.length===0){\n        container.innerHTML = '<p>No orders for your products yet.</p>';\n        return;\n    }\n\n    sellerOrders.forEach(order=>{\n        const card = document.createElement('div');\n        card.className='card';\n        // find customer name\n        const cust = users.find(u=>u.id===order.customerId);\n        const custName = cust ? cust.name || cust.email : 'Unknown';\n        // list only items that belong to this seller\n        const myItems = order.items.filter(it=>it.sellerId===sess.userId);\n        const itemsHtml = myItems.map(it=>`<li>${it.name} (x${it.quantity}) – ₹${it.price.toFixed(2)} each</li>`).join('');\n        // status dropdown\n        const statusOptions = ['Placed','Packed','Shipped','Delivered'];\n        const selectHtml = statusOptions.map(st=>`<option value=\"${st}\" ${st===order.deliveryStatus?'selected':''}>${st}</option>`).join('');\n        card.innerHTML = `\n            <p><strong>Order ID:</strong> ${order.orderId}</p>\n            <p><strong>Date:</strong> ${new Date(order.orderDate).toLocaleString()}</p>\n            <p><strong>Customer:</strong> ${custName}</p>\n            <p><strong>Items:</strong></p>\n            <ul>${itemsHtml}</ul>\n            <p><strong>Status:</strong> \n                <select class=\"statusSelect\">${selectHtml}</select>\n                <button class=\"btn saveBtn\">Save</button>\n            </p>\n        `;\n        container.appendChild(card);\n        const select = card.querySelector('.statusSelect');\n        const btn = card.querySelector('.saveBtn');\n        btn.addEventListener('click', function(){\n            const newStatus = select.value;\n            // simple forward-only check (optional)\n            order.deliveryStatus = newStatus;\n            // persist\n            const allOrders = storage.get(storage.keys.orders) || [];\n            const idx = allOrders.findIndex(o=>o.orderId===order.orderId);\n            if(idx>-1){\n                allOrders[idx] = order;\n                storage.set(storage.keys.orders, allOrders);\n                alert('Order status updated');\n            }\n        });\n    });\n})();"}}]}
