{"step_index":97,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T04:25:01Z","model":"gpt-oss-120b-medium","input_tokens":47459,"cache_read_tokens":3839,"output_tokens":1121,"content":"**Phase 3 – Seller Workflow is now implemented.**  \n\nBelow is a concise inventory of everything that was added or modified, the functionality that is now available, and any minor notes.\n\n---\n\n### 📁 Files Added / Modified (relative to the repository root)\n\n| Path | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **seller/dashboard.html** | Seller home page showing welcome, product counts, order count, recent orders, quick links. |\n| **seller/dashboard.js** | Dashboard logic: totals, recent orders, session check. |\n| **seller/add-product.html** | Form for sellers to create a new product. |\n| **seller/add-product.js** | Handles form submission, saves product with `status: 'pending'`, associates with logged‑in seller. |\n| **seller/manage-products.html** | Lists only the logged‑in seller’s products. |\n| **seller/manage-products.js** | Allows edit (via prompts) and delete of own products; displays approval status and any rejection remarks. |\n| **seller/manage-orders.html** | Shows orders that contain any of the seller’s products. |\n| **seller/manage-orders.js** | Lists those orders, shows customer name, items belonging to the seller, and lets the seller update the order status (`Placed → Packed → Shipped → Delivered`). |\n| **seller/reports.html** | Simple placeholder page for sales reports. |\n| **seller/reports.js** | Computes total orders and revenue for the seller and displays a static summary. |\n| **seller/** (folder) | Holds the above HTML & JS files. |\n| **assets/js/main.js** | Unchanged except for earlier home‑page rendering; still builds navigation based on session role. |\n| **assets/js/auth.js** | Unchanged – provides login/registration & session handling. |\n| **assets/js/storage.js** | Unchanged (seed data already present). |\n| **assets/js/checkout.js**, **orders.js**, **dashboard.js**, etc. | Unchanged – customer functionality remains intact. |\n| **assets/css/style.css** | Unchanged – retains the blue‑and‑white design. |\n| **README.md** | Already contains demo credentials; no changes needed. |\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Features that now work\n\n| Feature | Status |\n|---|---|\n| **Seller login protection** – all seller pages redirect to `login.html` if the session is missing or not a seller. | ✅ |\n| **Seller Dashboard** – welcome name, total products, approved/pending product counts, total orders, recent 3 orders, quick navigation links. | ✅ |\n| **Add Product** – form with name, description, category (populated from `categories`), price, stock, image URL. Saves product to `ecom_products` with `status: 'pending'` and associates `sellerId`. Shows confirmation message. | ✅ |\n| **Manage Products** – lists only the seller’s own products, displays status and any rejection remark, provides **Edit** (prompts) and **Delete** buttons. Edit cannot change approval status (cannot self‑approve). | ✅ |\n| **Manage Orders** – lists orders that contain at least one product belonging to the logged‑in seller. Shows order ID, date, customer name, items (only those belonging to seller), and a status dropdown with a **Save** button. Updates order’s `deliveryStatus` in `localStorage`. | ✅ |\n| **Reports** – simple summary: total orders and total revenue for the seller, displayed on the reports page. | ✅ |\n| **Navigation Bar** – automatically shows “Seller” link for logged‑in sellers via `main.js`. | ✅ |\n| **Data persistence** – all seller actions (product creation, edits, deletions, order status changes) are stored in `localStorage`. | ✅ |\n| **No interference with existing customer pages** – login, product browsing, cart, checkout, and order history continue to function exactly as before. | ✅ |\n| **Responsive layout** – uses existing CSS grid and utility classes; works on desktop and mobile. | ✅ |\n\n---\n\n### 🐞 Minor notes / possible refinements (optional)\n\n| Issue | Comment |\n|---|---|\n| **Edit UI** – uses `prompt()` dialogs for simplicity (good for a beginner project). | Could be replaced with a proper modal/form later. |\n| **Category editing** – when editing a product the category is changed by entering the *category ID* directly. | Not user‑friendly, but acceptable for the demo. |\n| **Status forward‑only check** – currently any status can be selected; a real system would enforce logical progression. | Not required for this basic project. |\n| **No image upload** – sellers provide an image **URL** rather than uploading a file (keeps the project static). | Works within the static‑site constraints. |\n| **Reports page** – displays only a static summary; charts are omitted to keep it beginner‑friendly. | Satisfies the “simple report” requirement. |\n\n---\n\n### 📋 Next step\n\nAll seller functionalities are now in place while preserving the existing customer workflow.  \n\nIf everything looks good, we can move on to **Phase 4 – Administrator Workflow** (admin dashboard, user management, product approvals, category management, reports).  \n\nPlease let me know if you’d like any adjustments to the seller pages, or give the go‑ahead to start the administrator phase."}
{"step_index":98,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-17T04:50:38Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nMASTER PROMPT: COMPLETE E-COMMERCE SHOPPING WEBSITE\nAct as a senior frontend developer and software architect.\nI am developing a college-level E-Commerce Shopping Website. I have already started this project and implemented the initial foundation, Customer Workflow, and Seller Workflow.\nYour task is to inspect the existing project, preserve all working functionality, complete the remaining modules, and deliver a fully functional beginner-friendly static website.\nDo not start a new project. Continue developing the existing project.\n1. PROJECT REQUIREMENTS\nTechnology Stack\nUse only:\nHTML5\nCSS3\nVanilla JavaScript\nBrowser LocalStorage for demo data storage\nStrictly do not use:\nPHP\nMySQL\nXAMPP\nNode.js\nReact\nAngular\nVue\nBootstrap\nBackend servers\nExternal authentication services\nReal payment gateways\nThe final website must be deployable directly using GitHub Pages.\nDesign Requirements\nMaintain the existing blue-and-white design.\nThe website should have:\nClean and professional appearance.\nSimple navigation.\nConsistent buttons and forms.\nResponsive desktop and mobile layouts.\nClear tables and dashboard summaries.\nAppropriate product images.\nSimple typography.\nConsistent spacing.\nAvoid excessive gradients, neon colors, unnecessary animations, oversized cards, and complicated designs.\nKeep the project suitable for a beginner-level college submission and viva explanation.\n2. PROJECT PHASES\nOrganize the complete project into these six phases.\nPHASE 1 – PROJECT FOUNDATION AND PUBLIC WEBSITE\nInspect and preserve the existing implementation.\nExpected public pages:\nindex.html\nabout.html\ncontact.html\nlogin.html\nregister.html\nproducts.html\nproduct-details.html\nExpected common JavaScript files:\nassets/js/main.js\nassets/js/auth.js\nassets/js/storage.js\nassets/js/products.js\nFeatures:\nHomepage with website logo and navigation.\nHomepage banner and introductory content.\nProduct categories.\nFeatured and latest approved products.\nProduct search.\nProduct browsing.\nProduct details.\nCategory and price filtering.\nCustomer and seller registration.\nLogin and logout.\nRole-based navigation.\nResponsive design.\nOnly approved products should appear in the public product listing.\nDo not recreate existing pages unnecessarily.\nPHASE 2 – CUSTOMER WORKFLOW\nPreserve the existing customer implementation and verify it.\nCustomer pages:\ncustomer/dashboard.html\ncustomer/cart.html\ncustomer/checkout.html\ncustomer/orders.html\ncustomer/profile.html\nFeatures:\nCustomer dashboard.\nWelcome message and order summaries.\nBrowse approved products.\nSearch and filter products.\nView product details.\nAdd products to cart.\nUpdate product quantities.\nRemove products from cart.\nCalculate subtotal and total.\nValidate product stock before checkout.\nSelect payment method:\nUPI\nCard\nCash on Delivery\nPlace orders.\nReduce stock after successful order placement.\nGenerate an order ID.\nView order history.\nTrack order status.\nView and edit profile details.\nPayment must be simulated. Never collect or store real card details or claim that a real payment was processed.\nCustomer order status should reflect seller order updates.\nPHASE 3 – SELLER WORKFLOW\nPreserve the existing seller implementation and verify it.\nSeller pages:\nseller/dashboard.html\nseller/add-product.html\nseller/manage-products.html\nseller/manage-orders.html\nseller/reports.html\nFeatures:\nSeller dashboard.\nAdd new products.\nEdit existing products.\nDelete own products.\nUpdate price and stock.\nSelect product category.\nProvide product image URL.\nSubmit products for administrator approval.\nDisplay pending, approved, and rejected statuses.\nDisplay rejection remarks.\nView orders containing the seller's products.\nUpdate order delivery status:\nPlaced\nPacked\nShipped\nDelivered\nView basic sales reports.\nSellers must only manage their own products and order items.\nDo not allow sellers to approve their own products.\nCalculate reports dynamically using LocalStorage rather than displaying hardcoded summaries.\nPreserve mixed-seller order data correctly.\nPHASE 4 – ADMINISTRATOR WORKFLOW\nCreate or complete the following pages:\nadmin/dashboard.html\nadmin/manage-users.html\nadmin/manage-categories.html\nadmin/product-approval.html\nadmin/orders.html\nadmin/reports.html\nCreate the corresponding JavaScript files.\nA. Admin Dashboard\nDisplay:\nTotal users.\nTotal customers.\nTotal sellers.\nTotal products.\nApproved products.\nPending products.\nTotal orders.\nTotal sales.\nRecent orders.\nAll values must be calculated dynamically.\nB. Manage Users\nFeatures:\nDisplay registered users.\nSearch users by name or email.\nFilter users by role.\nView customer and seller accounts.\nDelete customer or seller accounts with confirmation.\nPrevent deletion of the currently logged-in administrator.\nPrevent deletion of the only administrator account.\nNever display passwords.\nC. Manage Categories\nFeatures:\nAdd categories.\nEdit categories.\nDelete categories.\nDisplay all categories.\nPrevent duplicate category names.\nWarn before deleting categories used by products.\nD. Product Approval\nFeatures:\nDisplay pending products.\nDisplay approved products.\nDisplay rejected products.\nShow seller information.\nShow product name, category, price, and stock.\nApprove pending products.\nReject pending products.\nRequire rejection remarks.\nSave approval status and remarks.\nMake approved products visible to customers.\nKeep rejected products hidden from customers.\nE. Manage Orders\nFeatures:\nDisplay all customer orders.\nSearch by order ID or customer name.\nFilter by delivery status.\nView order details.\nDisplay customer information.\nDisplay products and quantities.\nDisplay order total.\nDisplay payment method and payment status.\nDisplay delivery status.\nDo not accidentally overwrite seller-specific item statuses in mixed-seller orders.\nF. Admin Reports\nDisplay dynamically calculated:\nTotal users.\nTotal customers.\nTotal sellers.\nTotal products.\nTotal approved products.\nTotal pending products.\nTotal orders.\nTotal sales.\nDelivered orders.\nOrders still in progress.\nRecent orders.\nKeep reports simple and beginner-friendly.\nDo not add complicated charts or analytics.\nPHASE 5 – CUSTOMER REVIEWS AND RATINGS\nImplement the review and rating functionality.\nCreate or update the necessary customer and product pages and JavaScript files.\nFeatures:\nCustomers can review products they have purchased.\nCustomers can submit reviews only after the relevant product has been delivered.\nAllow customers to provide a rating from 1 to 5 stars.\nAllow customers to enter written comments.\nSave reviews in LocalStorage.\nDisplay submitted reviews on the relevant product details page.\nDisplay the average rating for each product.\nDisplay the number of reviews.\nAllow customers to view their submitted reviews.\nPrevent duplicate reviews for the same product and order.\nValidate ratings and comments.\nUpdate product rating information dynamically.\nAdd rating-based product filtering if it fits the existing product listing without making the interface complicated.\nReviews must be associated with the correct customer, product, and order.\n3. NOTIFICATIONS\nImplement a simple LocalStorage-based notification feature if one does not already exist.\nCustomers should receive notifications when:\nAn order is placed.\nAn order is packed.\nAn order is shipped.\nAn order is delivered.\nAn order is cancelled, if cancellation is supported.\nDisplay notifications in the customer dashboard.\nDo not implement email, SMS, or third-party notification services.\n4. DATA STORAGE AND COMPATIBILITY\nThis is extremely important.\nBefore changing anything, inspect the existing assets/js/storage.js and all current JavaScript files.\nReuse the existing LocalStorage keys and data structures wherever possible.\nExisting keys may include:\necom_users\necom_products\necom_orders\necom_categories\nUse consistent structures for:\nUsers\nProducts\nCategories\nCart items\nOrders\nOrder items\nReviews\nNotifications\nDo not rename existing LocalStorage keys without a genuine technical reason.\nDo not break the existing customer or seller workflows.\nUse a consistent order structure so that customer, seller, and administrator pages display the same order information.\nHandle orders containing products from multiple sellers correctly.\nValidate:\nProduct price.\nProduct stock.\nRequested quantity.\nProduct approval status.\nUser role.\nReview eligibility.\nRequired form fields.\n5. DEMO ACCOUNTS\nPreserve the existing demo accounts if they are already present.\nExpected demo credentials:\nAdministrator:\nEmail: [admin@shopdemo.com](mailto:admin@shopdemo.com)\nPassword: Admin@123\nSeller:\nEmail: [seller@shopdemo.com](mailto:seller@shopdemo.com)\nPassword: Seller@123\nCustomer:\nEmail: [customer@shopdemo.com](mailto:customer@shopdemo.com)\nPassword: Customer@123\nDo not create duplicate accounts every time the website loads.\nSeed demo data only when required.\n6. SECURITY AND STATIC WEBSITE LIMITATIONS\nImplement basic client-side validation and role-based page protection for demonstration purposes.\nImportant:\nLocalStorage authentication is not production-grade security.\nLocalStorage data is stored in the individual browser.\nIt does not provide centralized multi-user data sharing.\nDo not claim that client-side role checks provide secure server authorization.\nDo not claim that the website supports real online payment processing.\nDo not store actual payment credentials.\nClearly document these limitations in the README.\n7. COMPLETE TESTING\nAfter all phases are implemented, test the entire website.\nAuthentication\nValid login.\nInvalid login.\nCustomer registration.\nSeller registration.\nLogout.\nRole-based page protection.\nProduct Management\nSeller adds a product.\nNew product receives Pending status.\nAdmin approves the product.\nApproved product appears in public listings.\nAdmin rejects another product.\nRejection remark appears in seller dashboard.\nSeller edits and deletes own products.\nShopping and Orders\nCustomer adds a product to cart.\nCustomer changes quantity.\nCustomer removes a product.\nCheckout validates stock.\nInsufficient stock prevents order placement.\nSuccessful order reduces stock.\nCustomer can view order history.\nSeller can view relevant orders.\nSeller updates delivery status.\nCustomer sees the updated status.\nAdmin can view all orders.\nReviews\nCustomer cannot review an undelivered product.\nCustomer can review a delivered product.\nReview appears on the product details page.\nAverage rating updates correctly.\nDuplicate reviews are prevented.\nAdministrator\nAdmin can manage users.\nAdmin can manage categories.\nAdmin can approve and reject products.\nAdmin can view all orders.\nAdmin reports show correct values.\nGeneral\nNavigation links work.\nAll JavaScript files load correctly.\nNo broken relative paths.\nNo unnecessary console errors.\nWebsite works on desktop and mobile.\nExisting functionality is preserved.\nDo not claim a test passed unless you actually execute and verify it.\n8. FINAL PROJECT STRUCTURE\nMaintain a clean project structure similar to:\necommerce-shopping-website/\n│\n├── index.html\n├── about.html\n├── contact.html\n├── login.html\n├── register.html\n├── products.html\n├── product-details.html\n│\n├── customer/\n│ ├── dashboard.html\n│ ├── cart.html\n│ ├── checkout.html\n│ ├── orders.html\n│ └── profile.html\n│\n├── seller/\n│ ├── dashboard.html\n│ ├── add-product.html\n│ ├── manage-products.html\n│ ├── manage-orders.html\n│ └── reports.html\n│\n├── admin/\n│ ├── dashboard.html\n│ ├── manage-users.html\n│ ├── manage-categories.html\n│ ├── product-approval.html\n│ ├── orders.html\n│ └── reports.html\n│\n├── assets/\n│ ├── css/\n│ │ └── style.css\n│ ├── js/\n│ │ ├── main.js\n│ │ ├── auth.js\n│ │ ├── storage.js\n│ │ ├── products.js\n│ │ └── other required JavaScript files\n│ └── images/\n│\n└── README.md\nYou may keep additional existing files if they are necessary.\n9. README DOCUMENTATION\nCreate or update README.md with:\nProject title.\nProject introduction.\nProject objectives.\nTechnologies used.\nFeatures.\nAdministrator, seller, and customer modules.\nProject folder structure.\nDemo login credentials.\nHow to run the website locally.\nHow LocalStorage is used.\nHow to deploy using GitHub Pages.\nStatic website limitations.\nDo not describe PHP, MySQL, XAMPP, or a backend as technologies used in the final implementation.\n10. GITHUB PAGES DEPLOYMENT\nPrepare the project for GitHub Pages.\nRequirements:\nKeep index.html in the repository root.\nUse relative paths for CSS, JavaScript, and images.\nAvoid absolute local computer paths.\nEnsure navigation works after deployment.\nEnsure customer, seller, and admin pages work through GitHub Pages.\nDo not require a backend server.\nDo not create unnecessary configuration files.\nDo not overwrite or delete existing GitHub repository content.\nIf GitHub authentication or deployment access is unavailable, prepare the project and provide exact manual deployment instructions.\n11. FINAL DELIVERY\nAt the end:\nInspect the entire project.\nFix broken links and file paths.\nCheck all role-based navigation.\nCheck LocalStorage consistency.\nTest the complete customer-to-seller-to-admin workflow.\nFix errors without unnecessarily redesigning the website.\nUpdate README.md.\nPrepare the project for GitHub Pages deployment.\nProvide a final report containing:\nAll completed phases.\nFiles created.\nFiles modified.\nFeatures implemented.\nTests actually performed.\nTests that could not be performed.\nRemaining bugs or limitations.\nExact steps to deploy the project on GitHub Pages.\nIMPORTANT FINAL INSTRUCTIONS\nContinue from the existing project